---
// Candidates/src/pages/privacy.astro
import '../styles/global.css';
---
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content="Privacy policy for the Wyoming 2026 Voter Guide." />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex" />
    <title>Privacy Policy — Wyoming 2026 Voter Guide</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="page-shell">
      <header class="site-header" aria-label="Candidates voter guide">
        <a class="brand-mark" href="/" aria-label="Candidates home">
          <span class="brand-mark__rule"></span>
          <span>
            <span class="brand-mark__project">The Integrity Project</span>
            <strong>Wyoming 2026</strong>
            <small>Primary Voter Guide</small>
          </span>
        </a>
      </header>

      <section class="privacy-content">
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="meta">Effective Date: September 3, 2025 &mdash; Last updated: August 13, 2026</p>

        <p>The Wyoming 2026 Voter Guide is a public civic project
        operated by Skovgard for Senate. This policy explains how information is handled on this site.</p>

        <h2>Information Collected</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>The voting address you enter for ballot lookup. This address is used only to match your legislative
          district and return the races on your ballot. It is not stored, linked to your identity, or used for
          any other purpose.</li>
          <li>GPS coordinates, if you choose to use the location button. These may be logged anonymously in
          aggregate to improve district-matching accuracy. They are not linked to your identity.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Bot Protection &mdash; Cloudflare Turnstile</h2>
        <p>
          The ballot lookup form on this site uses <strong>Cloudflare Turnstile</strong>, an invisible security
          service that verifies visitors are human without displaying a visible CAPTCHA. Turnstile runs silently
          in the background. It does not use cookies for verification and does not collect personal information
          on our behalf.
        </p>
        <p>
          By using the ballot lookup form, you acknowledge that Cloudflare may process certain technical signals
          from your browser in accordance with the
          <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/en-gb/turnstile-privacy-policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            Cloudflare Turnstile Privacy Addendum
          </a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Voice Guide (optional)</h2>
        <p>
          This site offers an optional "Start Voice Guide" feature that reads navigation choices aloud and can
          accept a limited set of spoken commands, such as "Find my ballot" or "Browse races." It is off by
          default and only starts if you select it.
        </p>
        <p>
          Voice commands use your browser's built-in speech-recognition service, not a service we operate.
          How your audio is processed depends on your browser and device. This site does not intentionally
          store audio, voice transcripts, or recognized commands &mdash; not in your browser's local storage, not
          in analytics, and not in any of our databases. Recognition only runs for a single short listening
          session at a time; the microphone is never left continuously active.
        </p>
        <p>
          Address information entered or spoken through the Voice Guide is used the same way as address
          information typed directly into the ballot lookup form &mdash; see "Information Collected" above. The
          Voice Guide never submits an address for lookup without an explicit confirmation step.
        </p>
        <p>
          If your browser does not support speech recognition or speech synthesis, the Voice Guide's help
          content and every navigation option remain available as ordinary on-screen buttons.
        </p>

        <h2>Email &amp; Recovery Links</h2>
        <p>This site sends email in two situations, both optional and neither tied to an account or login:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Candidate questionnaire link.</strong> A candidate can enter the email address on file with
            their official filing to receive a private link to complete their questionnaire. The email you type is
            only ever compared against the address already on file &mdash; it is never used to send mail to an
            address that doesn't match a filing. This link remains valid through the primary election.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Ballot list recovery link.</strong> A voter can optionally email themselves a link to restore a
            saved list of races and candidate picks on a different device. Unlike the candidate link above, this
            email address is not checked against anything &mdash; whatever address is entered receives the link.
            The link and the saved list behind it expire automatically 24 hours after being sent and are deleted
            after that; no persistent identity or account is created.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Both emails are delivered through <strong>Resend</strong>, a third-party email delivery service, solely
          to send the message itself.
        </p>

        <h2>Sharing</h2>
        <p>We do not sell or share address or lookup data with third parties. Candidate and race data displayed
        on this site is drawn from publicly available Wyoming Secretary of State filings.</p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>Skovgard for Senate &middot; 5685 Hanly Mills Wy, Casper, WY 82604 &middot;
        <a href="mailto:skovgard2026@gmail.com">skovgard2026@gmail.com</a></p>

        <p class="back-link"><a href="/">&larr; Back to voter guide</a></p>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="site-footer" aria-label="Campaign disclaimer">
      <span class="site-footer__rule"></span>
      <p>Paid for by Skovgard for Senate</p>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  .privacy-content {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 48px 20px 80px;
  }
  .privacy-content h1 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
    color: var(--color-navy, #0f2742);
  }
  .privacy-content h2 {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 2rem 0 0.5rem;
    color: var(--color-navy, #0f2742);
  }
  .privacy-content p,
  .privacy-content li {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: #374151;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }
  .privacy-content ul {
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .privacy-content a {
    color: #b22234;
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  .meta {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: #6b7280;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }
  .back-link {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
</style>
